      "id": "42656283-17c2-487c-953d-6506fd724abd",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### Generate a bunch of random students task\n\nLooking at one random student at a time isn't very efficient. So let's build an ***array*** of students that we can test all at once. An array is an indexed sequence of information. For example, a `String` object with the data \"CTIS 210\" can be thought of as containing an array of `char` values that can be visualized as\n\n|index|character|\n|:--:|:--:|\n|0|`'C'`|\n|1|`'T'`|\n|2|`'I'`|\n|3|`'S'`|\n|4|`' '`|\n|5|`'2'`|\n|6|`'1'`|\n|7|`'0'`|\n\nWe can declare and initialize such an array with the following statement.\n\n```java\nchar[] stringChars = {'C', 'T', 'I', 'S', ' ', '2', '1', '0'};\n```\n\nNow suppose we want to declare an initialize an array of Guilford credit values for five students. We can do that with the following statement:\n\n```java\ndouble[] studentGuilfordCredits = {28, 12, 44, 76, 32};\n```\n\nExtend that in the following code cell to declare arrays for transfer credits, other credits, and whether the student is studying away. Note that the last array should be declared as `boolean[]`. Then display them using the statement given as a model.\n",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "42656283-17c2-487c-953d-6506fd724abd"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "12a6cb23-4a24-45b5-adb6-e1f2ce7f3667",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// Add additional arrays for all the attributes\n\ndouble[] studentGuilfordCredits = {28, 12, 44, 76, 32};\n\n\nSystem.out.println(\"Guilford Credits: \" + Arrays.toString(studentGuilfordCredits));",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "d0c4597e-1f64-4de9-b1e6-e1d9ae006866",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "#### Create a really large number of random students task\n\nThat's not yet particularly random, and it's not that many students, so suppose we now want to build an array with 18,357 students, each with a random value for each attribute. That's a repetitive task that we need to run a specified number of times, so we will use a counting loop. The next few cells will work through these steps.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "d0c4597e-1f64-4de9-b1e6-e1d9ae006866"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "8b164351-a3e9-472f-ade0-b6231847598a",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "##### Declaring arrays with a specified size.\n\nWe an array where we can store 18,357 values of Guilford credits. We're going to use a random number generator to generate those values, but for now we just want to reserve the memory to do that. Here's the code for that.\n\n```java\ndouble[] studentGuilfordCredits = new double[18357];\n```\n\nIn the next code cell, add this line, and then do the same for the other three attributes that we've been using.",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "8b164351-a3e9-472f-ade0-b6231847598a"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "224ac629-28a5-4e02-b751-6fdb4fc54eae",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// Declare arrays for the attributes\n\n",
