    {
      "id": "f4f6d473-542a-4b54-a84a-626e85a646f7",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "##### Writing a loop to fill the array\n\nA counting loop needs three elements: Initialize, test and update.\n\n* Initialize: We'll declare a variable `index` and set it equal to zero. \n* Test: We'll want to run the loop as long as `index` is smaller than the size of the array.\n* Update: We should increase `index` by one each time the loop body runs.\n\nThat leads to the following code.\n\n```java\nint index = 0;\nwhile (index < 18357) {\n    studentGuilfordCredits[index] = rand.nextDouble(0, 92);\n    index++;\n}\n```\n\nEnter this code into the next cell. To test it, print out any value of the array. For example, `studentGuilfordCredits[24]` will give the value of the 25th element of the array. Try several different values of the array.\n\nAfter that, add code that fills an array for each of the other attributes. Test all the generation of values by printing out the attributes for a single student. ",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "f4f6d473-542a-4b54-a84a-626e85a646f7"
      }
    },
